+# ---- [MP8] Manual table tuning (user decision 2026-08-16 - the user adjusts coordinates themselves, and only the 4 new tables move) ----
+#
+# Why this exists - the layout has already been overturned twice (generic top-up → corner pairs → ring), and every round was
+# agent guesses coordinates → package build → user checks in the real game → overturned. With the knobs in the user's hands that back-and-forth goes away.
+#
+# The save file lives in user://, which is %APPDATA%\Godot\app_userdata\Machine Party\.
+# ⚠️ All 8 instances **share the same user:// directory** (pitfall #15) — this time that's a good thing.
+# Save once and all 8 instances read the same copy next match, so layouts naturally can't differ between machines.
+const MP8_LAYOUT_FILE: String = "user://mp8_gun_layout.txt"
+
+const MP8_EDIT_STEPS: Array[float] = [1.0, 0.5, 0.1]
+const MP8_EDIT_YAW_STEP: float = 15.0
+
+# The **safe lower bound** for the distance between two table centers, derived from the three boxes measured by probe36 (don't lower it)
+#   Player InteractArea = cylinder radius 1.00, hanging about 1 m in front of the body
+#   Workstation InteractArea = Box 2.00 × 3.60 (half depth 1.80, half diagonal 2.06)
+# When standing at your own table, the center of your reach circle is about 1.8 m from that table's center, with circle radius 1.0,
+# and the other table's trigger box reaches out another 1.8~2.06 → 1.8 + 1.0 + 2.06 ≈ 4.86.
+# Below that you get "table B is also in interacts_in_range while using table A".
+# With the vanilla `return` in place, the result is **this player can't do anything**.
+# After switching to `continue` (see the manufacture_gun_player.gd patch) only the no-physical-overlap requirement is left,
+# but this line is still kept as a **yellow light**. Tables this close don't look good anyway.
+const MP8_MIN_DESK_GAP: float = 4.9
+
+# Query height for "is there room to stand here" when placing spawn points. Only the waist-up band is checked (y≈0.68~2.08).
+# ⚠️ Don't hug the floor. Near the floor the query picks up the floor collider itself, so **everywhere inside the field reads as occupied
+# while outside the walls reads as empty**, and players get placed outside the walls (the user hit this in testing on 2026-08-16).
+# This height band is the same rule as "standing spots only look waist-up, y 0.75~2.0", settled after three calibration rounds in probe35/37.
+const MP8_SPOT_PROBE_Y: float = 1.375
+# Scan steps for candidate directions - 0°, ±15°, ±30°, ±45°, ±60°, ±75° — **at most ±75°, so it can't scan outward**.
+# Beyond ±90° means facing away from the field center = moving toward outside the walls, which is exactly the pitfall above.
+const MP8_SPOT_SWEEP: int = 11
+
